{"id": "EUVD-2026-103618", "enisaUuid": "49ba02ee-3e8d-39ad-a07d-dfc0d67d4f2c", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nnet: skbuff: fix pull-bound underflow in skb_checksum_setup_ipv6()\n\nskb_maybe_pull_tail() subtracts skb_headlen(skb) from the unsigned max\nargument and passes the result to __pskb_pull_tail() as a signed int.  The\nfunction does not ensure that max is at least skb_headlen(skb).\n\nThis can happen while parsing IPv6 extension headers when an skb already\nhas a linear area larger than MAX_IPV6_HDR_LEN.  Once the parser needs data\nbeyond the linear area, max - skb_headlen(skb) wraps and is converted to a\nnegative delta.  __pskb_pull_tail() then passes that negative length to\nskb_copy_bits(), where it can become a very large copy length.\n\nPass the requested length itself as the pull bound at the three\nextension-header call sites, so the delta can no longer go negative.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:58", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9c4e432132a97b82edf28fa172c39f743e6bfb26", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/718747afa5463d9cc5fd9a09f03b2a492edd9b78", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a0ad0473c09d2e947aecac5c82e637ec85924b12", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2da5ed3d8c75e1b729a21b6d3beaed415e263f6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6c28c31f051dbf49c71ba7ab7bb9bc905fa1d14b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cfa643f2ca36c6f913fe1a2ceb12412ebb0fd962", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d7f474226809471dc7877435e9c492cc914df0bf", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3b4e0b0c008a8c1b474730248cd5b873026c74bd"], "aliases": ["GHSA-23rj-wp7f-556g", "CVE-2026-98573"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "00ec07bc-6557-3335-885e-661bf083d0c5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.189"}, {"id": "0272b015-d123-3dc9-b322-a2bad29633ee", "product": {"name": "Linux"